  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Schema v2 now carries compact terminal p-radical/full-rank-minor witnesses for every resolved squared word prime after final HNF rebasing. The immutable ordinary-Python decoder independently reconstructs order arithmetic, nilradicals, radical lattices, and selected multiplier equations before certifying complete results. Partial and arbitrary-prime results retain locally certified primes but remain globally incomplete. The durable benchmark separates native construction, generated-host transfer, independent verification, and end-to-end time.",
    "risks": [
      "Independent verification remains far above the 2ms public gate: six-case warm end-to-end medians are 67.1ms, 10.5ms, 11.0ms, 36.8ms, 208.3ms, and 623.5ms.",
      "The portable tier passed 275 of 276 with the shared FLINT prefix; its sole failure is the unrelated verified-native-bundle relocation test, which intentionally rejects an externally redirected prefix. Without the prefix, three unrelated GF(2) compilation tests cannot find FLINT headers.",
      "Current-revision Linux arm64, Windows x64, and macOS arm64 lifecycle validation remains external to this worktree."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Do not wire the resource into the public maximal-order engine at current verifier costs.",
      "Run the focused schema-v2 lifecycle witness on Linux arm64 and native Windows x64 before any public adoption; macOS arm64 remains an external CI requirement.",
      "If future profiling finds a safe verifier acceleration, retain immutable source binding and independent nilradical/full-rank verification rather than trusting native rank claims."
    ]
  }
